Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Per-project access control: PROJECTS:VIEW:ONLY_ASSIGNED

No Payne fork. A user whose role has the new instance permission
PROJECTS:VIEW:ONLY_ASSIGNED can only see and change projects they manage or
are crew on. Everyone else, including server admins, is unaffected.

All logic is in src/common/libs/Auth/nopayneProjectScope.php:
- a request guard, run at the end of headSecure.php and apiHeadSecure.php
  (and in api/file/index.php), refuses any request naming an out-of-scope
  project directly or through a child record (assignments, payments, crew,
  notes, vacancies, applications, project files)
- nopayneProjectScopeWhere() hooks limit every project listing (sidebar,
  project list page and API, search, assets page dropdown, calendar,
  ledger, user page, clients totals, vacancies, sub-projects)
- nopayneProjectScopeRedact() hides other projects' names where an asset or
  crew member's other bookings are shown

New businesses' Administrator role, and the e2e "full access" role, don't
get the restriction. No schema changes.

E2E: authenticated/nopayne-project-scope.spec.ts (with setup/nopayneProjectScope.php).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
